From: ferlzc <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
Subject: [PATCH] insane.bbclass: fix bb.note() format in match_line_in_files

The FileNotFoundError handler in match_line_in_files() formats a message
that has no conversion specifier with d.getVar('PN'), so the handler
itself raises "TypeError: not all arguments converted during string
formatting" and fails do_patch. It triggers when a file disappears while
the unimplemented-ptest scan globs the source tree, and shows up as a
random, non-reproducible do_patch failure (seen on linux-mainline).

Drop the stray format argument so the note is logged and the check is
ignored, as the comment above it intends.

---
diff --git a/meta/classes-global/insane.bbclass b/meta/classes-global/insane.bbclass
index 9004a9d..f1c57af 100644
--- a/meta/classes-global/insane.bbclass
+++ b/meta/classes-global/insane.bbclass
@@ -1357,7 +1357,7 @@ python do_qa_patch() {
         except FileNotFoundError:
             # pathlib.Path.glob() might throw this when file/directory
             # disappear while scanning.
-            bb.note("unimplemented-ptest: FileNotFoundError exception while scanning (disappearing file while scanning?). Check was ignored." % d.getVar('PN'))
+            bb.note("unimplemented-ptest: FileNotFoundError exception while scanning (disappearing file while scanning?). Check was ignored.")
             pass
         return False
 
